    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0106" n="96" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg96"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/874: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sparks</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-09T16:00:00-05:00">December 9, 1941—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:51 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>246. The following is translation of the pertinent part of a note received today
                    from Minister for Foreign Affairs.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d111-f1"/></p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“In view of the unjustifiable aggression of the Japanese Government against
                        American possessions in the Pacific the Republic of Haiti faithful to its
                        policy of friendship and complete understanding with the United States of
                        America and in accord with the Pan-American doctrines of continental
                        solidarity has placed itself alongside of the sister republic in declaring
                        war against the Japanese Empire.</p>
                    <p>I would be grateful to you to bring this fact to the knowledge of your
                        Government and to request the Department of State to be good enough to
                        communicate it to the Embassies of the United States at <pb facs="0107"
                            n="97" xml:id="pg97"/> Vichy, London and Rome charged with Haitian
                        interests and to communicate it also to Mr. Leon Robert Thebaud, our
                        Minister to the Holy See.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sparks</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
